80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 54 0 R
/T (        This project investigates whether traditional machine-learning regression models can predict land surface temperature from historical meteorological and temporal information. The target variable is land surface temperature, selected because temperature is an important environmental indicator with implications for agriculture, water resources, and human well-being.)
/E (        This project investigates whether traditional machine-learning regression models can predict land surface temperature from historical meteorological and temporal information. The target variable is land surface temperature, selected because temperature is an important environmental indicator with implications for agriculture, water resources, and human well-being.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 54 0 R
/T (        The project uses hourly ERA5 reanalysis data from the Copernicus Climate Data Store for a location in Giza, Egypt. Three regression approaches are compared: Linear Regression, XGBoost, and Random Forest. The models are evaluated using a chronological train/test split and three-fold cross-validation.)
/E (        The project uses hourly ERA5 reanalysis data from the Copernicus Climate Data Store for a location in Giza, Egypt. Three regression approaches are compared: Linear Regression, XGBoost, and Random Forest. The models are evaluated using a chronological train/test split and three-fold cross-validation.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 54 0 R
/T (        The final experiments identify Random Forest as the strongest of the tested models. Hyperparameter tuning does not improve the held-out test score, but it substantially reduces the gap between training and testing performance, providing a less overfit model with similar generalization performance.)
/E (        The final experiments identify Random Forest as the strongest of the tested models. Hyperparameter tuning does not improve the held-out test score, but it substantially reduces the gap between training and testing performance, providing a less overfit model with similar generalization performance.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
