306 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project uses hourly ERA5 reanalysis data from the Copernicus Climate Data Store for a location in Giza, Egypt. Three regression approaches are compared: Linear Regression, XGBoost, and Random Forest. The models are evaluated using a chronological train/test split and three-fold cross-validation.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 232 0 R
/Prev 270 0 R
/Next 271 0 R
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Title (The objective is to build a regression model that estimates land surface temperature from meteorological)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 272 0 R
/Next 343 0 R
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Title (The prediction target is land surface temperature \(`t2m` in the source dataset\). The model uses surface pressure, precipitation, wind characteristics, and temporal features such as hour, month, quarter, day of week, and year.The project also compares several model families to determine whether nonlinear ensemble methods provide an advantage over a simple linear baseline.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 272 0 R
/Prev 343 0 R
>>
endobj
