/Title (The Random Forest feature-importance analysis indicates that surface pressure and hour of day are among the most influential predictors, followed by temporal features such as month. Precipitation has relatively low importance compared with the other selected features. These feature-importance values should be interpreted as model-specific importance rather than direct evidence of physical causation or statistical correlation. In particular, a feature being important to the Random Forest does not by itself establish that it causes temperature changes.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 346 0 R
>>
